From d664528851e91cbeb2dc4a761eaac5c4ff32d524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sleepy <sleepy@example.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:05:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] build: reconcile additive layer with the 7.3 base (fix
 build)

Three stale-API overlaps from the 7.2 additive layer that break the 7.3
build, fixed so the wannabe tree compiles:

- mm/page_alloc.c: MARIE 0.10.5's unguarded thrash-aware no-progress block
  references ac->last_refaults (a field the 7.3 header hunk failed to add).
  Since CONFIG_LRU_MARIE is not enabled in this preview, restore the base
  should_reclaim_retry() logic and drop the __alloc_pages_slowpath baseline.
  (MARIE needs a proper 7.3 port before it can be re-enabled.)
- amdgpu_amdkfd_gfx_v12.c: 9045 (KFD CU-occupancy) applied twice - remove the
  duplicate function block.
- dcn42b_soc_bb.h: 1116/1117 (dcn42b translator) duplicates the base
  dml2_dcn42b_max_ip_caps definition - remove the extra copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
